# ============================================================================
# NOTEBOOK 62 — CELL 21N
# OFFICIAL CG OPTION OBJECT SCHEMA + SEMANTIC FIELD AUDIT
# ============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# Cell 21M proved that the official cg package exposes authoritative enums,
# including cg.api.OptionType:
#
#     7  -> PLAY
#     8  -> ATTACH
#     9  -> EVOLVE
#     12 -> RETREAT
#     13 -> ATTACK
#     14 -> END
#
# However, the same integer values also occur in other cg enums.
# Therefore integer equality alone is NOT sufficient evidence that the
# observed runtime option values are OptionType values.
#
# This cell performs a READ-ONLY forensic audit of:
#
#     cg.api.Option
#     cg.api.SelectData
#     cg.api.OptionType
#     cg.api.SelectType
#     cg.api.SelectContext
#     cg.game.battle_select
#
# It attempts to determine:
#
#   1. the declared structure of Option and SelectData,
#   2. annotations / dataclass fields / namedtuple fields / slots,
#   3. constructor signatures,
#   4. source-code references to OptionType,
#   5. source-code references to option.type / option_type,
#   6. whether battle_select establishes authoritative enum semantics.
#
# SAFETY
# ------
# READ ONLY.
# No model modification.
# No retraining.
# No submission-directory modification.
# No fit()/predict() calls.
# No battle execution.
# No semantic mapping will be guessed.
# ============================================================================

from pathlib import Path
